
Poka-Yoke for Programs
1. Introduction
Poka-Yoke ka meaning hai “mistake-proofing”, yani aise safeguards lagana jo program mein common mistakes ko prevent ya handle kar sakein.

Real life mein examples:

Fixture jo workpiece ko sirf ek hi direction mein fit hone deta hai.


Connector jo ulta plug nahi ho sakta.


Programming mein bhi hum Poka-Yoke ka use karke program ko unexpected input aur common errors se protect kar sakte hain.

What I learned
Maine seekha ki program mein errors aana normal hai, lekin un errors ko properly handle karna important hai. Error ko hide karna solution nahi hai; humein uska actual cause samajhna chahiye.


2. Error Messages / Tracebacks
Python mein jab program mein error aata hai, to Python ek error message/traceback deta hai.

Error message ko insult nahi, balki inspection report ki tarah dekhna chahiye.

Traceback se humein usually pata chalta hai:

Error kis type ka hai


Error kis line par hua


Error ka possible reason kya hai


Important Rule
Traceback ki last line pehle padho, kyunki last line generally error ka species/type batati hai.

Uske baad line number dekho aur identify karo ki problem exactly kahan hui.


3. Types of Errors I Learned
Error Type

Meaning

Example

