4. TypeError
Meaning
TypeError tab aata hai jab hum incompatible data types ke saath operation karne ki koshish karte hain.

Example
age = 25

text = "30"


print(age + text)


Yahan integer aur string ko directly add nahi kar sakte.

What I learned
Maine seekha ki operation karne se pehle mujhe check karna chahiye ki dono values compatible data types ki hain ya nahi.


5. ValueError
Meaning
ValueError tab aata hai jab data ka type acceptable ho, lekin uski actual value valid na ho.

Example
number = float("twentyfive")


Python string ko float mein convert kar raha hai, lekin "twentyfive" valid numerical value nahi hai.

What I learned
Maine seekha ki correct data type hone ke baad bhi value invalid ho sakti hai.


6. NameError
Meaning
NameError tab aata hai jab hum kisi aise variable ya name ko use karte hain jo Python ko pata hi nahi hai.

Example
print(total)


Agar total pehle define nahi kiya gaya hai, to NameError aayega.

What I learned
Maine seekha ki variables ko use karne se pehle properly define karna zaroori hai.


7. KeyError
Meaning
KeyError dictionaries ke saath commonly aata hai jab requested key dictionary mein available nahi hoti.

Example
parts = {

    "P101": "Bolt",

    "P102": "Nut"

}


print(parts["P105"])


P105 dictionary mein nahi hai, isliye KeyError aayega.

What I learned
Maine seekha ki dictionary se data access karte waqt key ke available hone ka dhyan rakhna chahiye.


8. IndexError
Meaning
IndexError tab aata hai jab hum list/string ke aise index ko access karte hain jo exist nahi karta.

Example
items = ["Bolt", "Nut", "Screw"]


print(items[5])


List mein index 5 exist nahi karta.

What I learned
Maine seekha ki list ya string access karte waqt valid index use karna chahiye.


9. AttributeError
Meaning
AttributeError tab aata hai jab kisi object ke andar aisa method ya attribute access kiya jaye jo exist nahi karta.

Example
P.make_part()


Agar object P ke paas make_part() method nahi hai, to AttributeError aayega.

What I learned
Maine seekha ki kisi object ke available methods aur attributes ko samajhna important hai.


10. ZeroDivisionError
Meaning
Jab kisi number ko zero se divide karne ki koshish ki jaati hai, Python ZeroDivisionError deta hai.

Example
total = 10

count = 0


average = total / count


Yahan division by zero ho raha hai.

What I learned
Maine seekha ki division karne se pehle denominator ko check karna chahiye.


11. try / except
Python mein errors ko handle karne ke liye hum try aur except ka use kar sakte hain.

Basic Structure
try:

    # Code that may cause an error

except SomeError:

    # Code to handle that error


Example
try:

    age = int(input("Enter your age: "))

except ValueError:

    print("Please enter a valid number.")


Agar user "abc" enter karta hai, program directly crash hone ke bajay proper message show karega.


12. Two Important Rules of try / except
Rule 1: Keep the try block short
try ke andar sirf wahi code rakhna chahiye jahan error expected hai.

Bad approach:

try:

    # Bahut saara unrelated code

    ...

except:

    ...


Better approach:

try:

    age = int(input("Enter age: "))

except ValueError:

    print("Invalid age.")


Why?
Agar try block bahut bada hoga, to pata lagana difficult ho jayega ki actual error kahan hua.


Rule 2: Name the exception you expect
Specific exception ko catch karna better practice hai.

Example:

try:

    number = int(input("Enter a number: "))

except ValueError:

    print("Invalid number.")


Yahan hum specifically ValueError handle kar rahe hain.


13. The Bare except: Trap
Bare except: ka matlab hai ki almost koi bhi exception catch ho sakta hai.

Example:

try:

    number = int(input("Enter number: "))

except:

    print("Something went wrong.")


Iska problem ye hai ki agar program mein koi unexpected bug ya typo ho, to bare except us error ko bhi hide kar sakta hai.

Why is this dangerous?
Agar error hide ho gaya, to:

Bug identify karna difficult ho sakta hai.


Program wrong behaviour kar sakta hai.


Important error message disappear ho sakta hai.


Developer ko actual problem ka pata nahi chalega.


Better approach
try:

    number = int(input("Enter number: "))

except ValueError:

    print("Please enter a valid number.")


What I learned
Maine seekha ki bare except: avoid karna chahiye jab tak uski genuinely zarurat na ho. Humein preferably wahi exception catch karna chahiye jise hum expect kar rahe hain.


14. Poka-Yoke in Programming
Programming mein Poka-Yoke ka main purpose hai:

Common mistakes ko prevent ya safely handle karna.

For example, agar user se number input lena hai:

try:

    quantity = int(input("Enter quantity: "))

except ValueError:

    print("Quantity must be a number.")


Yeh program ko unexpected input se protect karta hai.

Is tarah try/except ek guard ki tarah kaam karta hai.


15. Error Handling ka Correct Approach
Error handling karte waqt mujhe ye steps follow karne chahiye:

Error message ko calmly read karo.


Traceback ki last line dekho.


Error ka type/species identify karo.


Line number check karo.


Error ka actual cause samjho.


Sirf expected exception ko catch karo.


try block ko short rakho.


Error ko blindly hide mat karo.


Input validation aur appropriate guards use karo.


Program ko test karke dekho ki guard properly kaam kar raha hai.



16. Practical Activity – Fit the Guards
Activity mein mujhe apne crash log se ek real error lena tha aur us program ko mistake-proof karna tha.

Example
Problem:

number = int(input("Enter a number: "))


Agar user "hello" enter karega, ValueError aayega.

Mistake-proof version:

try:

    number = int(input("Enter a number: "))

except ValueError:

    print("Please enter a valid number.")


Learning
Maine seekha ki real program ke error ko identify karke uske according specific guard lagana chahiye.


17. Teach-Back / Hostile Input Testing
Guard lagane ke baad program ko sirf normal input se test nahi karna chahiye.

Humein hostile/unexpected input bhi dena chahiye.

Example:

Agar program number expect karta hai:

25


ke saath-saath test karna chahiye:

hello

twenty

25.5

blank input


What I learned
Maine seekha ki ek guard tabhi reliable hai jab hum usse different unexpected inputs ke saath test karein.

Agar test ke dauran koi naya error milta hai, to humein uske liye appropriate guard add karna chahiye.


18. Key Takeaways
Aaj ke topic se maine ye important concepts seekhe:

Poka-Yoke means mistake-proofing.


Programming mein errors ko properly handle karna important hai.


Error messages ko inspection report ki tarah read karna chahiye.


Traceback ki last line pehle read karni chahiye.


Python mein different errors ke different meanings hote hain.


try/except errors ko safely handle karne mein help karta hai.


try block ko short rakhna chahiye.


Expected exception ko specifically name karna chahiye.


Bare except: errors ko hide kar sakta hai, isliye iska careless use nahi karna chahiye.


Guards ko unexpected/hostile inputs ke saath test karna chahiye.


Error ko hide karna aur error ko properly handle karna same thing nahi hai.


Good programmers errors se panic nahi karte; woh traceback ko read karke problem identify karte hain.


Final Learning
I learned that a good program is not just a program that works with correct input. A good program should also be prepared for incorrect or unexpected input. Poka-Yoke helps us build these safety guards, while proper exception handling helps us understand and manage errors without hiding real problems.

